  <has_step rdf:resource="#Step_112948"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Longboard or Skateboard Truck Maintenance</has_title>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_standard_length_screwdriver">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_utility_knife">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40116">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/5ykCkyYbhtLJq3pQ.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Peel off the paper backing from the sheet of grip tape. Make sure you do not fold or wrinkle the grip tape.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40117">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/fKHoBuRqWocnKMoy.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Center the sheet of grip tape evenly over the top of the skateboard deck.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40118">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/1fXDOaYc5vusTjHw.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/PlP1ZxrNnBHRpTfE.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Starting from the very middle and moving outward, firmly press down on the grip tape while smoothing out any air bubbles that start to form.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40124">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_standard_length_screwdriver"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_utility_knife"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/iJYC4hy21QgfZJoW.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/PuG6OEF3uEQFOZ6M.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use a screwdriver to scrape along the edges of the skateboard.  This will remove some of the grip around the edges making the trimming process easier on you and your equipment. You can use the utility knife to cut a perpendicular line in the excess grip tape if it is resisting the screwdriver too much.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40125">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_utility_knife"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/qLaYqEGaZ5XZXAeS.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/RbehKKuCWMP4Xyf5.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/vXHPnE4jnEFHIXLv.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use a utility knife to begin cutting around the edge of your skateboard to remove excess grip tape. Angle your knife towards the inside of the skateboard to make it easier to cut a straight line. Be careful when using the utility knife and always keep it pointed away from yourself and others.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40127">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/H4nQrBF3CQsctskU.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Once you have removed all of the excess grip tape, you can use the scraps to sand the edges of your cut to smooth out any small inconsistencies. Use caution when sanding as the grip tape can become heated.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40509">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_utility_knife"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/i6AiDoH26J6NhMNa.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If air bubbles persist, gently use a utility knife to poke a small hole in the grip tape at the center of the bubble and press out the air. Be careful when using the utility knife and always keep it pointed away from yourself and others.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40510">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_standard_length_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/2gJK4KFOW2p1VNGj.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/1LoFoIik14YPgXLo.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After you have finished applying your grip tape, you can use a small screwdriver to poke holes where your truck hardware will be installed.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_3_8_wrench">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40134">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/2TYtKDPmQeuJqPXN.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/bhoRXBg6VeC4yWlD.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Insert bolt hardware through the factory drilled holes from the top side of the skateboard. If you have a riser and would like to install it, please reference the [guide|11251|Wheel Bite Prevention] guide.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40137">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/bqBWAkDGk1ZSWRIS.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Slide the truck onto the four protruding bolt hardware screws, while using your hand to prevent the screws from popping out the top of the skateboard.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40138">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/AHnNo2PDNdtxkbsQ.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Hand tighten the nut hardware onto all four bolts.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40140">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_hex_key_allen_wrench"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/BXtLQ1eRNVI2gflh.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">While holding the nuts on the bottom side of the skateboard in place with the 3/8" wrench, tighten the screws from the top side of the skateboard with a screwdriver.  Tighten the screws in a diagonal pattern until the head of the screw sinks slightly into the grip tape. Repeat steps 1 - 6 to install the second truck.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_compressed_air">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_lint-free_cloth">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_paper_towels">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_metal_can">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40270">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_paper_towels"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/pvCa6gZGWuRGKgDY.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FibGU6NaBtoNIEQu.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Protect your work area such as a desk with paper towels or newspaper. Be sure that the environment in which you are performing this work is well ventilated and uncarpeted. Remove your bearings from your wheels, if they are not removed already.  Please reference the [guide|11243|Wheel Installation] guide for information on how to properly remove bearings.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40274">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/VCImVhKQpNQJeJVR.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Set out your two metal containers and fill them with just enough of your Citrus Based Cleaner to fully submerge one bearing.  One container will be for cleaning and one will be for rinsing. Be sure to wash your hands when finished dealing with the Citrus Based Cleaner as these chemicals can be harsh on skin. Gloves are optional but recommended.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40275">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_utility_knife"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/aymuhBTw3a2devPH.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/NhWlloYy4P3MwYFP.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove ONE shield from your bearing using the small point of a utility knife.  This will allow the chemicals to enter the bearing more freely when the bearing is submerged.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40276">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FDVAPQ3Tg3Buqsfw.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/deVe6m3xAenrrPXy.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Submerge your bearing in the cleaning container for 15 - 20 seconds to allow  the solvent to soak into the bearing.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40277">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/rHZOrkir3TbGHfZZ.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/cfHtGgAhIj2uF2Ir.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After submerging the bearing, remove it from the cleaning solution and begin to scrub off any dirt or grease with a toothbrush. You may also scrub the shield that you removed so that it can be cleaned as well.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40278">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/BGJvlXZqRTM2HEJA.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/JS3qCm4IQae1qQGm.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/wN5NQNnjStXURWEX.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">When finished scrubbing the bearing, rinse it in FRESH cleaning solution until there is no dirt or old lubricant in the bearings.  Then set this bearing aside. Repeat steps 4 - 7 for your remaining seven bearings.  Be sure to continue to refresh your rinsing solution if it becomes too dirty.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40280">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_compressed_air"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/AluhEYEgZXrJAqvN.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Once you have cleaned all of your bearings, use a can of compressed air to blow any of the cleaning solution out of the bearings. Do this as soon as possible to prevent rust from forming.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40281">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_lint-free_cloth"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/GbrKZQvgkdgU5WFU.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Carefully blot your bearing with a lint-free cloth to remove any excess cleaning solution. Be careful not to get any fibers stuck in the bearing.  One tiny piece of hair or lint can severely reduce the performance of your bearing.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40282">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/cXHkuvfPmFdkjDxL.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/5tmoDLbSVIrWaOM1.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After you have thoroughly dried your bearing, you can now relubricate the bearing.  To do this, simply coat all inside parts with the lubricant and spin the bearing in order to disperse the lubricant fully. Make sure to spin the bearing immediately after the lubrication process. Warning!  The bearing lubricant is harmful if swallowed and can cause skin irritation.  Be sure to keep away from open flames because the lubricant is flammable.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_40283">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_lint-free_cloth"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/YSSyJyoE5fEmaF2O.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/YcpgUJqgcrYWfrxJ.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Carefully wipe the bearing with a lint-free cloth that is slightly oily.  After this you can replace the protective shield by simply pressing it into place. Repeat steps 8 - 7 for all other bearings.  After you have completely relubricated all of your bearings, see the [guide|11243|Wheel Installation] guide to help you install your bearings into your wheels.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_needlenose_pliers">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50213">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_smart_wrench"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ifmDQqJo4qXTTSHN.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/cbPdJBx5K1jUXEXU.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use the half inch wrench to remove the nut on each wheel. Then remove each wheel. Be careful not to lose the washers that sit between the nut and wheel, they are small and hard to find after you lose them.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50214">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_needlenose_pliers"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/H4MPt5PTu4kqb6NY.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/luTIxvBN1a5ksiDQ.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/Ja45o1FGPX44NyJe.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use needle nose pliers to remove the bearings from both sides of each wheel.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50215">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tOK3Zb6Vkf2xHvPE.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/WYHAOMGo6steUPUU.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Place the bearings in soapy water and let them soak for 5 minutes.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50216">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/crTDVMZohtSGVfbZ.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tDyScC1QTTilHXGy.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/Zad5tSP3IwWkPnhV.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Wipe off the dirt from each bearing and dry them thoroughly with a paper towel.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50217">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/c62DxNIQDAfn41Xe.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/3Q6w6ukGElj1dv3A.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Apply a few drops of lubricant to the inner portion on both sides of each bearing. Spin the bearings and wipe off any extra lubricant that has not settled in.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50218">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/3LCqyCQ6KWTTKeXV.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/Ulf3YdSn1MKJOrbG.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/aJMEWBAV2EMOu6Fg.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Push the bearing into the wheel by applying even pressure with your thumb.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50219">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/qmBcU2mZuYiKcdAF.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/b3jOseHj5rSwyLjl.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/GsKBUaHcUl2eNoUh.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Spin the wheel to make sure that the bearings are properly aligned and running smoothly.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_50220">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_smart_wrench"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/TVmIoDBhQNjNsuwd.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/VdJInMYtfOsQCdVt.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/TcJTuxInlWERgKKb.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Place the wheel on the axle followed by washer and then the nut. Tighten the nut with your fingers as much as you can first and then use the wrench to finish the job. Do not tighten the nut too much or else the wheel will not be able to spin. You should be able to slightly shake the wheel up and down along the axle.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_toothbrush">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_cup">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_91700">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_smart_wrench"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/o2J5CyNljwhQ6G1N.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/oLFqwwEWfDQEFQhZ.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Turn your wrench to the left to remove the wheel nut. Take the wheel off of your trucks by pulling. Keep all nuts and spacers in separated, designated areas. Wear gloves. You are working with messy materials such as gasoline.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_91729">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_flathead_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/HJQOlTIkysAOUUZg.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/X66QHjDYGuEmGgma.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Firmly lever the bearing out using your screwdriver. Do not be overly forceful to avoid scratching the bearing.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_91772">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_cup"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/eh6VYgwQUf6ZQRV5.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Soak the bearing in a cup with premium gasoline for 5 minutes. Soak each bearing separately so none are lost or dented.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_92446">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/HnbMRAJERpbMEGH2.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ZEGvQBMAK2dADHGZ.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/gMInQFiAWRQIOtYM.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Take the bearing out of the gasoline and remove one side of the outside plastic locks by applying pressure on the inner ring and prying up. Make sure you can clearly see and access the ball bearings.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_91780">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_toothbrush"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/PZ1TQCsR34Y1aO1S.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use your toothbrush to clean the bearings by using a gentle back and forth scrubbing motion. Rinse the bearing with water and let dry for 5 minutes.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_91788">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/2mnmCTGxTV2WB2dj.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/Uk1mDGKQyHDxT4b5.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Once dry, pick up your bearings with two fingers and drop 2 drops of skateboard lubricant into the bearing. Spin the bearings immediately to spread the lubricant evenly.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_92455">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/OZLnLiSHbUiFWHgK.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/paEddqv1wUITUBsw.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/bngAmmTeANdWoEhf.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use a paper towel to remove excess lubricant. Replace the plastic guard.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_adjustable_wrench">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_soap_bar">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_rubbing_alcohol">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_cloth">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109417">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_adjustable_wrench"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/wdZntXqDaAMEIFoB.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/qLjLLY4G1tXQDAw4.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Start by placing your board on its top so that you can access the trucks. Use an adjustable wrench to remove the large nut that is screwed onto the end of the kingpin.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109463">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/qOTvIdP1hAcUtKHp.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/sufrdu1j1YrKSBTM.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/mH1V1LNMp4xqMIBB.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Take apart the trucks by removing the parts in this order: washer #1, bushing #1, metal hangar, bushing #2, washer #2 To remove the hanger, wiggle it off of the kingpin (large bolt), then lift it out of the pivot cup. Make sure you remember the order of the parts! Take a picture if you need to, or simply refer to the other side of the board for the correct truck setup.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109465">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_needlenose_pliers"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/McryIOFoByValEoR.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/DtBZPN1CqqMasRVK.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Using pliers (needle nose would work best), take out the small pivot cup where the metal hangar was resting. Place all of the pieces aside. Make sure to not lose any, as one missing piece means your board can't be put back together.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109467">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_rubbing_alcohol"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tZYYiP1pwReV4ang.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/WPEykgtXTEcDJPZF.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Apply a small amount of rubbing alcohol on a cloth or sheet of paper towel. Clean the pivot cup and bushings. Rinse the pivot cup and bushings by running the items through hot water.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109469">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ni1LOTKVRE6gseHr.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/t1nf264Eb4PUgJwN.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Take a small pot and bring a moderate amount of water to a rolling boil. Place the bushings in the boiling water and cover the pot. Boil the bushings for 10-15 minutes. Boiling water is hot! Make sure to be careful when putting in the bushings.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109470">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_needlenose_pliers"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/4OEDD5vPA3TTDC3K.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Using the pliers, take the bushings out of the pot. If you are not comfortable with the softness just yet, boil the bushings for 5 more minutes. Let the bushings cool for 2 minutes.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109475">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_soap_bar"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/1LDTmCwoNrEjogbV.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/B2IVyBwT5fmtMQ4k.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/V1TyZHYFHtfys4OC.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Take the edge of a soap bar and rub the bottom and top of the bushings until a film of soap is visible. Using a knife, cut small soap shavings and place a small amount in the pivot cup.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109728">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/KtKfUB2KOUcuAK2p.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/TZTYLBQcDAKvk6GG.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ihkulIcJVuoETDKE.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reassemble the trucks by first placing the pivot cup back in its hole Place the washers, bushings, and hanger on the large bolt, and then tighten the nut last.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_109732">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/6pjrDAYTwlMB6yvW.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/IjtfqfvQWAvnDIZ1.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Once the trucks have been reassembled, step on the board and test the turning sensitivity. If turning is hard or requires you to lean too much, loosen the nut. If turning is too loose and not stable, tighten the nut. You have successfully tuned your longboard with your "new" bushings and it's ready to ride!</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_basic_pliers">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112900">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_phillips_2_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/QnvVUefnaNOC54pE.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/RRCvKZUP1BegEV6H.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use a Phillips/flat head screw driver, along with a skate tool or set of pliers, to loosen the nuts which fasten the trucks to the deck.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112906">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/UJHpqZTZFlWTptQS.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use your fingers to fully loosen and remove the nuts from the bolts. Nuts are small and easy to lose track of.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112914">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/gfETpj4t4xRcRKfV.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/CWM51LB25wiCGM5H.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/uiUvDYL26TF3ByVK.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use your hands to remove the trucks from the deck. Make sure the kingpin is facing outward, If the kingpin is not properly reinstalled, the trucks will fail to perform properly.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112918">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/y6YOIQFYSepTYbVr.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the truck raiser if applicable.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112921">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/O1kUDua53VWTT4UQ.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ReDgXy1sjcHaIMyD.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the bolts from the factory drilled holes on the deck. Note that the bolts are small and easy to lose track of.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112923">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/uMpPQZGEMxBdBiMb.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Clean the deck with a moist cloth or cleaning solution.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112925">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/JtTXmItLexHkT4yS.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Clean the trucks with a moist cloth or cleaning solution.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112931">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/VYIPPpQgkIfrhwwb.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tyskjXQ1MqfKeyJH.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Clean the hardware by either soaking it in cleaning solution, or by manually cleaning it with a moist cloth.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112937">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/2yXcpEScAKPlp1Ux.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Repeat steps 1-7 with the second truck.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112946">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/hgGTPAuRk1MlWCEl.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After re-installation, check and confirm that all the bolts and nuts are tight. The bolts should be slightly submerged in the wood of the deck Over tightening the bolts can cause them to strip. Failure to tighten the bolts and nuts properly may lead to improper performance.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_112948">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/U4IU4LTFsuaEKVKh.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/sBIxBipd6v3fRRLC.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After re-installing the trucks, check and confirm the kingpin is facing outward. Failure to do this will cause the longboard's functions to be inverted, which may lead to personal injury.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

