<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_195629">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/CG5IsO2TQsSc6jlw.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/GEQJLA1Bwlq6AI4e.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The battery is accessible through the back of the drone. Press the tabs on both sides of the white stripe to pull the battery out.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_195630">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_ph000_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/6LYSh3hTYvNJQM16.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/6IYCQ5dYgONVyZjr.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/lxPWnxso22yqcTkk.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Now that the battery is out, remove the screws starting with the four smaller ones on the top part of the battery. After this, remove the last four on the side. Make sure to keep track of where each screw came from. There should be one 7 mm Phillips head screw, three 6 mm Phillips head screws, and four 5 mm Phillips head screws. There is another screw that is located where the arrow is pointed. You will need to take the other screws out first before you can get to this one.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_195631">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/lUG2ceLr6LugK2DE.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/IpjpNK2NsSthDIHv.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the top piece, and gently pry the two halves apart. Divide the sticker if necessary.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_195633">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/RTGqiFPtioYauZwA.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/gvVQ2nQ6VTgdkkxl.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The battery is now removable from its container. During reassembly, make sure the outlet is returned to its holder and faces the correct direction.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Tool_phillips_screwdriver_j000">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Tool"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198253">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/5qBAwmdXjemAaHWX.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/DB2wtvgipmnqVp2J.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the 4x 7mm Phillips head screws on the outside of the shell, and the 2x 5mm Phillips head screws from the middle, then remove the back part of the housing. Remove the two hidden screws at the bottom, and the white power button. There will be 6x 7 mm Phillips head screws, and 2x 5 mm Phillips head screws in total.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198254">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/NcwrFfCHPKT2LBju.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/rJFOijSsJsRQyN5j.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/EffVR4UmRlNtSphC.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Unplug all the cords from the circuit boards. Carefully slide the main body off of the arms.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198256">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FQyWiNgK5FCTYWDW.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/OMMxyJcCJQyAEQKY.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/2hmHvT3JHE1K2eWB.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove all screws from all four arms, and the screws on either side of the center. The screws on the arms are 7mm. The screws on the motor are 9mm. Remove the 5mm screw holding the rotor onto the drone. '''Note''' There should be 22x 7 mm Phillips head screws, 8x 9 mm Phillips head screws and 1x 5 mm Phillips head screw.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198257">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_opening_tool"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/BbXSDXmQpZmZQuJ2.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Gently pry apart the upper and lower part of the shell by working the opening tool along the middle seam.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198264">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/hBFGJm4EPrLRRbuD.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/uqYZeLdmidSeXX5U.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/A41aQeRqkpnCFSqn.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Unscrew the motor screws, and remove the motor. There will be 2x 6 mm Phillips head screws. Pry up the middle portion of the arm to access the cables.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198276">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/TnTE6YEQd2GxrNaA.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/lqqy1qSCyAFUKlGS.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the motor by unsoldering the cords from the main circuit board. The motor will either have blue and red cords, or black and white cords, with two of each kind on opposite sides of the drone. It is important that the new motor spins the same direction as the old one, and that you connect the leads to the correct port.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198832">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_ph000_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/kkvSocAoyKgXLQIl.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/okuEmaECCZv3HZ1h.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the 4x 7mm screws on the top and bottom, and the 2x 5mm screws from the middle,  then remove the back part of the housing. Remove the two hidden screws at the bottom, and the white power button. There will be 6x 7 mm Phillips head screws, and 2x 5 mm Phillips head screws.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198833">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/3yD5i21AejKAXSWI.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/HLOOviLZSWfNtRtH.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/gPH6XCUjlCcLJNWZ.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Unplug all the cords from the circuit boards. Carefully slide the main body off of the arms.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_198828">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_ph000_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/ANqQGAdDcQuXn2WY.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/aPuaMVLnY5JdEpAB.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the four screws, and unsolder all cords on the circuit board. There will be 4x 4mm Phillips head screws. It is important to keep track of where the leads came from. Red/Blue and Black/White pairings belong to motors, whereas Black/Red pairings belong to lights. The ports are labeled on the board.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_199577">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_opening_tool"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/I2OuK6TGX5kUFHBp.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/QqmmVVpE1u2vrnE4.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/SBkYWhVvYK4yLYVP.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the phone slide from the virtual reality lens. Take the outside cover off using a plastic opening tool.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_199589">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/Lexhsd3eLxn41OLj.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/pTpbQDFHvMIYcdcj.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/dcfBFnQCF2KS3cX5.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove each screw from its place. Four screws will be 6mm Phillips head. Twelve screws will be 7mm Phillips head. Pull each bracket out so you can see the full lens case.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_199591">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_tweezers"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/JW5LTvFtIhNNnpSt.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/KSkA3AE2OHkwZ5pl.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/UTLSt2YoBnBCYDUT.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">You will need to remove the adjustable lens lever on top of the virtual reality lens. Using a tweezers, you will need to separate the tooth gears and remove them so the lens can fall freely out. Pull the lens case out from the front of the headset.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_199592">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/EbChR5j3dpiupfSN.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/y3PdyJnhPTJQDaTx.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To get the actual lens out, you will need to push the lens from the outside in with a little force to break the lens out of it's case.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

